I stand up with my phone.
"I want to show you my home," I say.
I turn the camera around.
"Look, this is my living room."
I walk into my kitchen.
"And here is my kitchen."
My father smiles on the screen.
Then I walk over to the window.
"Here is my window," I say.
"Your flat is small, Maya," my sister, Sofía, says.
I laugh.
"Yes, it is a small flat," I say.
"But it is nice."
"And it is mine," I think, and smile.
